Christian wrote:
>Other than making the game harder, why would anyone put the amulet on?
>You've got to include some benefits, too, I think..

As others have said, it's simply a way to make the game harder - an
extra conduct. Of the 16 characters I have played who have completed
the quest, 14 have ascended. I just wanted a way to introduce some
extra challenge into the end game. Why not just do conducts, you say?
Well I've been quite into speedrunning recently, but aside from that,
most conducts are based around removing parts of the game - scrolls of
genocide, polymorphing, wishes, the religion system... even all
weapons! - which IMHO removes some of the fun that those items provide.
This hard mode is a way to toughen up the game without removing any of
it.

